# The web/api apps were authored against a flat (yarn-style) node_modules and
# import some transitive deps directly (e.g. @dnd-kit/utilities, @tiptap/core).
# The RN/Expo toolchain in mobile/ has its own, much larger set of phantom
# transitive imports (e.g. @expo/metro-runtime) that only surface as bundler
# errors, not typecheck failures — so this stays a broad hoist rather than a
# hand-enumerated allowlist. The one exclusion: @types/react(-dom), which
# frontend and mobile both declare directly at different versions — hoisting
# it too created a real root-level copy *alongside* each package's own
# pnpm-store-linked copy, and TS treats those as structurally-identical but
# nominally different modules (broke radix-ui's `--radix-*` CSSProperties
# augmentation with "two different types with this name exist" errors).
public-hoist-pattern[]=*
public-hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react
public-hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react-dom
